-- title:
--   Supersingular maximal ideal of the j-chart at q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with the value of the generator $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$), and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the latter being the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the level-$\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ function field of conductor $q^2M'$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ (a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue map onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, together with a degree- and order-preserving map on places), assumed to be the coefficientwise reduction: every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is $R_0$-integral with residue the coefficientwise image under $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Fix $s\in W$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and put $A_0=A\cap k_0$; assume $\pi_0\in k_0$ lies in $A$, that $A_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Let $H_1$ be the intersection of $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ with the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$, let $K$ be the intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq k_0((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $k_0$ the coefficientwise image of the level-$H_1$ function field of conductor $q^2M'$, with $A_0\to K$ an algebra structure compatible over $k_0$, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series the coefficientwise image of $j_q$. Write $C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ for the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$, and assume the image of $j_q$ lies in $K$ and in $C$. Then there is a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ such that: the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $y$; for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, that is, every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$; and for every $g\in\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $R_0$-integral, is regular at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which $j_q$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equals the value at $s$ of that residue, the difference in $C$ of the image of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $y$.
--
--   This produces a supersingular closed point, in characteristic $q$, of the finite $j$-chart of the integral model over the small constant ring $A_0$ of the modular curve of level $H_1=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'\cap\ker((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times)$, specialising a prescribed supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ function field in characteristic $q$ and prescribing the reductions of all level-$M'$ functions regular there. It is the $q=2$ variant adapted to a diamond guard prime $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, and it feeds the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation rings and the inertia analysis at the level field used later in the argument.
